1
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,000
"The Last Oath"

2
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:04,100
(Episode 21: Self-experiment Record)

3
00:01:09,125 --> 00:01:10,125
Come in.

4
00:01:22,916 --> 00:01:23,916
He Yao.

5
00:01:23,958 --> 00:01:24,958
Are you all right?

6
00:01:27,916 --> 00:01:28,583
It's my fault.

7
00:01:28,791 --> 00:01:30,431
I didn't explain things clearly to A-Leh.

8
00:01:33,583 --> 00:01:34,083
It's fine.

9
00:01:34,416 --> 00:01:35,416
That's in the past.

10
00:01:35,583 --> 00:01:36,666
What brings you here?

11
00:01:41,916 --> 00:01:43,076
I want to continue the trial.

12
00:01:44,291 --> 00:01:45,583
So this is your brother.

13
00:01:51,916 --> 00:01:52,916
Lin Zai.

14
00:01:53,208 --> 00:01:55,291
I warned you about
the risks from the start.

15
00:01:55,333 --> 00:01:56,916
You barely survived it last time.

16
00:01:57,333 --> 00:02:00,000
Maybe we...
should call this off.

17
00:02:01,416 --> 00:02:02,416
No.

18
00:02:02,625 --> 00:02:03,666
I can take it.

19
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,750
He Yao, you can't give up either.

20
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,600
Don't you have someone you want to save?

21
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:13,083
You have someone to save, too.

22
00:02:14,625 --> 00:02:15,791
He Yao has a younger brother.

23
00:02:15,916 --> 00:02:17,249
He was bitten by a zombie, too.

24
00:02:17,250 --> 00:02:18,708
He's locked up in Casia right now.

25
00:02:20,291 --> 00:02:21,291
What a coincidence.

26
00:02:23,458 --> 00:02:24,458
A-Leh.

27
00:02:24,583 --> 00:02:25,708
You don't need to doubt me.

28
00:02:25,750 --> 00:02:28,083
Lin Zai and I share the same goal.

29
00:02:28,875 --> 00:02:29,875
Perhaps...

30
00:02:30,583 --> 00:02:31,708
you can't understand that.

31
00:02:34,541 --> 00:02:36,083
Whether I understand doesn't matter.

32
00:02:36,458 --> 00:02:38,583
Just make sure you're
actually doing research.

33
00:02:39,583 --> 00:02:40,708
So tell us.

34
00:02:41,333 --> 00:02:42,750
What's your next step?

35
00:02:42,916 --> 00:02:44,676
Do you need to draw
more of Lin Zai's blood?

36
00:02:48,708 --> 00:02:49,708
Not right now.

37
00:02:49,750 --> 00:02:51,083
I have a new protocol.

38
00:02:51,125 --> 00:02:52,445
But it requires some preparation.

39
00:02:52,750 --> 00:02:55,083
I'll let you know once
I confirm it's feasible.

40
00:02:58,416 --> 00:02:59,582
All you need to do right now

41
00:02:59,583 --> 00:03:01,291
is focus on getting your strength back.

42
00:03:01,916 --> 00:03:03,583
Maybe we're getting

43
00:03:05,208 --> 00:03:06,408
closer to curing your brother.

44
00:03:07,083 --> 00:03:08,083
Really?

45
00:03:08,708 --> 00:03:10,207
That's wonderful. Don't worry.

46
00:03:10,208 --> 00:03:11,458
I'll definitely be ready.

47
00:03:14,291 --> 00:03:15,291
Let's go.

48
00:06:24,708 --> 00:06:25,708
Where were you?

49
00:06:26,208 --> 00:06:27,250
Just went for a walk.

50
00:06:40,916 --> 00:06:41,916
What's on your mind?

51
00:06:44,500 --> 00:06:45,750
He Yao's younger brother...

52
00:06:46,083 --> 00:06:47,083
What's his name?

53
00:06:48,333 --> 00:06:49,333
He Yao's brother?

54
00:06:50,958 --> 00:06:52,083
I can't recall.

55
00:06:53,291 --> 00:06:54,291
I think it was...

56
00:06:54,750 --> 00:06:55,958
Chang-something.

57
00:06:57,416 --> 00:07:00,208
He Changhuan?

58
00:07:02,083 --> 00:07:03,083
I don't think so.

59
00:07:49,166 --> 00:07:50,708
Why were you so distracted earlier?

60
00:07:53,375 --> 00:07:54,375
It's nothing.

61
00:07:55,875 --> 00:07:57,458
You seem in good spirits today.

62
00:07:59,916 --> 00:08:00,458
Yeah.

63
00:08:00,916 --> 00:08:02,276
My brother might finally be saved.

64
00:08:02,750 --> 00:08:04,500
He Yao said the trial looks promising.

65
00:08:15,083 --> 00:08:16,083
Don't worry.

66
00:08:16,458 --> 00:08:17,458
No matter what happens,

67
00:08:17,583 --> 00:08:18,916
I'll look after myself.

68
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:20,500
I promise.

69
00:09:31,291 --> 00:09:32,291
Brother.

70
00:09:33,875 --> 00:09:35,000
I'm in so much pain.

71
00:09:36,333 --> 00:09:36,958
What's wrong?

72
00:09:36,958 --> 00:09:37,958
Where does it hurt?

73
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,000
Your head or your chest?

74
00:09:40,583 --> 00:09:41,583
It's just...

75
00:09:42,583 --> 00:09:43,916
I feel horribly stiff.

76
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,000
Untie me.

77
00:09:50,750 --> 00:09:52,083
Just let me move around.

78
00:09:55,916 --> 00:09:57,125
Just for a little bit.

79
00:09:57,916 --> 00:09:58,916
I promise,

80
00:09:59,458 --> 00:10:01,083
I won't do anything stupid.

81
00:10:11,500 --> 00:10:12,500
Brother.

82
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,000
I'm sorry.

83
00:10:14,750 --> 00:10:15,833
Last time,

84
00:10:16,875 --> 00:10:18,583
I was way too harsh.

85
00:10:20,125 --> 00:10:21,125
I know

86
00:10:21,708 --> 00:10:22,750
everything you do

87
00:10:23,416 --> 00:10:24,791
is for my own good.

88
00:10:37,708 --> 00:10:38,708
Take it easy.

89
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:41,000
Careful.

90
00:10:43,208 --> 00:10:44,416
But sometimes,

91
00:10:45,958 --> 00:10:48,333
I feel like we've gone too far.

92
00:10:49,375 --> 00:10:50,583
So far that

93
00:10:51,458 --> 00:10:53,291
we can't find our way back anymore.

94
00:11:01,750 --> 00:11:02,950
Changhuan, what are you doing?

95
00:11:04,750 --> 00:11:05,750
Potassium cyanide.

96
00:11:07,083 --> 00:11:08,583
This is deadly poison!

97
00:11:09,750 --> 00:11:11,470
Who the hell are you planning to use it on?

98
00:11:21,791 --> 00:11:22,291
You...

99
00:11:22,291 --> 00:11:22,958
Let go!

100
00:11:23,083 --> 00:11:23,750
Give it to me!

101
00:11:24,083 --> 00:11:25,083
Give it here!

102
00:11:25,250 --> 00:11:26,333
Let go of me!

103
00:11:26,416 --> 00:11:27,540
Let go of me!

104
00:11:27,541 --> 00:11:28,583
Give it to me!

105
00:11:30,750 --> 00:11:31,750
Give it back!

106
00:11:47,333 --> 00:11:48,458
Why did you stop?

107
00:11:51,958 --> 00:11:53,375
If you hate me this much,

108
00:11:54,750 --> 00:11:56,125
you might as well just bite me.

109
00:12:00,291 --> 00:12:01,291
Sometimes,

110
00:12:02,916 --> 00:12:04,500
I've thought about ending it all, too.

111
00:12:27,583 --> 00:12:28,583
Changhuan.

112
00:12:29,708 --> 00:12:31,083
Since you don't have the guts

113
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:33,541
to turn me into someone like you,

114
00:12:35,166 --> 00:12:36,916
then don't ever try to stop me

115
00:12:38,284 --> 00:12:40,159
from turning you back into someone like me.

116
00:12:56,625 --> 00:12:57,708
Come on, A-Leh.

117
00:12:58,208 --> 00:12:59,250
Let's arm wrestle.

118
00:13:00,291 --> 00:13:01,541
Don't go easy on me.

119
00:13:11,750 --> 00:13:12,500
Hey.

120
00:13:12,501 --> 00:13:13,621
Keep your eyes on the hands.

121
00:13:14,750 --> 00:13:15,750
Right.

122
00:13:45,833 --> 00:13:47,353
You really have recovered well lately.

123
00:13:48,083 --> 00:13:48,916
You know it.

124
00:13:48,917 --> 00:13:50,208
I'm taking you down next time.

125
00:13:50,666 --> 00:13:51,750
In your dreams.

126
00:13:52,416 --> 00:13:53,416
Lin Zai.

127
00:13:56,375 --> 00:13:57,457
The results of the new blood comparison

128
00:13:57,458 --> 00:13:58,958
and cell culture tests are in.

129
00:13:59,166 --> 00:13:59,791
How are they?

130
00:13:59,791 --> 00:14:00,791
Any progress?

131
00:14:02,833 --> 00:14:03,915
Preliminary results show

132
00:14:03,916 --> 00:14:04,708
that your serum

133
00:14:04,709 --> 00:14:06,249
neutralizes the virus in vitro

134
00:14:06,250 --> 00:14:07,791
better than whole blood alone.

135
00:14:07,875 --> 00:14:08,583
However,

136
00:14:08,584 --> 00:14:09,624
if we want to achieve

137
00:14:09,625 --> 00:14:11,499
deep neural repair and reversal,

138
00:14:11,500 --> 00:14:13,340
we might need components
with higher viability

139
00:14:13,708 --> 00:14:15,291
and stronger regenerative capacity.

140
00:14:16,083 --> 00:14:17,083
Such as...

141
00:14:17,541 --> 00:14:18,666
bone marrow stem cells.

142
00:14:21,916 --> 00:14:23,083
A bone marrow extraction?

143
00:14:23,416 --> 00:14:25,517
- Lin Zai's body has barely—
- I understand your concern.

144
00:14:25,541 --> 00:14:27,958
But based on my recent
observations and modeling,

145
00:14:28,083 --> 00:14:29,457
the zombie virus's erosion

146
00:14:29,458 --> 00:14:31,082
of the host's nervous system

147
00:14:31,083 --> 00:14:32,875
has an irreversible tipping point.

148
00:14:33,166 --> 00:14:34,416
Given your brother's condition,

149
00:14:34,583 --> 00:14:36,863
conventional serum infusions
are too slow to take effect.

150
00:14:37,750 --> 00:14:39,083
We can't afford to wait.

151
00:14:42,458 --> 00:14:43,375
All right.

152
00:14:43,375 --> 00:14:44,375
I can do it.

153
00:14:44,916 --> 00:14:46,396
As long as there's a glimmer of hope,

154
00:14:46,521 --> 00:14:47,646
I have to try.

155
00:14:47,795 --> 00:14:49,302
[The blackboard has something
about a survival compass written on it]

156
00:14:49,375 --> 00:14:50,375
Lin Zai.

157
00:14:51,958 --> 00:14:52,958
A-Leh.

158
00:14:52,959 --> 00:14:54,166
I know the risks.

159
00:14:54,458 --> 00:14:55,750
But my brother can't wait.

160
00:14:56,916 --> 00:14:57,957
Besides,

161
00:14:57,958 --> 00:14:59,458
I feel pretty good right now.

162
00:15:00,333 --> 00:15:01,333
Really.

163
00:15:15,541 --> 00:15:16,583
When do we start?

164
00:15:17,250 --> 00:15:18,541
If you're ready,

165
00:15:18,750 --> 00:15:19,791
we can do it right now.

166
00:15:24,083 --> 00:15:25,249
Okay.

167
00:15:25,250 --> 00:15:26,250
I'll go with you.

168
00:15:54,791 --> 00:15:55,791
Where's the anesthetic?

169
00:16:01,416 --> 00:16:02,416
I'm sorry.

170
00:16:02,916 --> 00:16:03,916
Couldn't find any.

171
00:16:04,083 --> 00:16:05,375
Are you kidding me?

172
00:16:06,291 --> 00:16:07,291
It's fine.

173
00:16:07,916 --> 00:16:08,916
I can handle it.

174
00:16:15,125 --> 00:16:16,250
Bite down on this.

175
00:16:30,750 --> 00:16:31,870
Whatever you do, don't move.

176
00:16:40,333 --> 00:16:41,125
Hold still.

177
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:42,250
Try not to move.

178
00:17:05,750 --> 00:17:06,750
All done.

179
00:17:32,750 --> 00:17:33,541
Lin Zai.

180
00:17:33,750 --> 00:17:34,851
Catch your breath for a bit.

181
00:17:34,875 --> 00:17:35,833
Once you're feeling better,

182
00:17:35,834 --> 00:17:36,954
head back and get some rest.

183
00:17:39,458 --> 00:17:41,208
I want to see how my brother's doing.

184
00:17:54,083 --> 00:17:55,083
We'll wait right here.

185
00:17:57,750 --> 00:17:58,750
It won't be that fast.

186
00:17:58,958 --> 00:17:59,999
I still need to centrifuge

187
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:01,290
and purify the sample.

188
00:18:01,291 --> 00:18:02,291
How long?

189
00:18:02,416 --> 00:18:03,583
At least forty minutes.

190
00:18:07,375 --> 00:18:08,083
Do what you need to do.

191
00:18:08,083 --> 00:18:09,083
I'll wait right here.

192
00:18:37,416 --> 00:18:38,500
What are you doing now?

193
00:18:39,083 --> 00:18:40,416
For Lin Zai's sake,

194
00:18:40,791 --> 00:18:42,083
I'm giving him a nutrient shot.

195
00:18:54,791 --> 00:18:56,083
Roll up his sleeve.

196
00:19:01,791 --> 00:19:02,791
Hold him still.

197
00:19:38,541 --> 00:19:39,541
Take care of him.

198
00:20:49,416 --> 00:20:50,416
Where are you going?

199
00:20:56,083 --> 00:20:57,083
Is it ready?

200
00:20:57,625 --> 00:20:58,291
Hurry.

201
00:20:58,291 --> 00:20:59,083
Hurry, He Yao!

202
00:20:59,166 --> 00:21:00,166
Save my brother, quick!

203
00:21:01,958 --> 00:21:04,083
The sample needs at least
half an hour of observation

204
00:21:04,458 --> 00:21:05,916
to confirm cell viability is stable.

205
00:21:06,333 --> 00:21:07,333
Injecting it now

206
00:21:07,916 --> 00:21:08,996
poses uncontrollable risks.

207
00:21:09,375 --> 00:21:11,575
Earlier you said forty minutes
was the processing time.

208
00:21:11,875 --> 00:21:12,833
Now we have to wait again?

209
00:21:12,834 --> 00:21:14,166
Science requires precision.

210
00:21:14,500 --> 00:21:15,708
If viability is insufficient,

211
00:21:15,791 --> 00:21:17,750
an injection could trigger rejection,

212
00:21:17,833 --> 00:21:19,233
and all our efforts will be ruined.

213
00:21:22,333 --> 00:21:23,853
Either inject it right in front of me,

214
00:21:24,750 --> 00:21:25,750
or

215
00:21:25,833 --> 00:21:27,433
I'm leaving with Lin Zai and the sample.

216
00:21:27,625 --> 00:21:28,625
Your choice.

217
00:21:29,583 --> 00:21:30,958
If you rush this

218
00:21:31,291 --> 00:21:32,582
and it fails,

219
00:21:32,583 --> 00:21:33,999
can you take responsibility?

220
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:36,458
Will you inject it or not?

221
00:21:46,916 --> 00:21:47,958
Fine.

222
00:21:48,666 --> 00:21:49,791
I'll inject it now.

223
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:05,666
Brother.

224
00:23:05,916 --> 00:23:06,916
Brother.

225
00:23:10,916 --> 00:23:11,916
Can you hear me?

226
00:23:13,250 --> 00:23:13,791
Brother.

227
00:23:14,208 --> 00:23:15,208
Brother.

228
00:23:15,250 --> 00:23:16,250
Can you hear me, Brother?

229
00:23:16,375 --> 00:23:17,416
It's me, Lin Zai, Brother!

230
00:23:17,583 --> 00:23:18,583
Brother.
